<li><strong>Renamed:</strong> baptised Johannes Leo de Medicis, 6 January 1520</li>
<li><strong>Wrote:</strong> an Arabic-Hebrew-Latin dictionary (5,500 Arabic entries), an Arabic translation of the Epistles of Paul, and the <em>Description of Africa</em>, completed 1526</li>
<li><strong>Later life:</strong> left Italy after the Sack of Rome, recorded in Tunis by 1532; died there around 1554</li>
</ul>
